\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Experiments on semisynthetic CIFAR-10 dataset. Median labeler accuracy represents the median of $p_i = \max _y \textup  {softmax}(\alpha f(x_i))_y$ on the training data. Results are averaged over $20$ trials, and vertical axes give mis-classification rate from (synthetic) ground-truth labels on held-out test set. Legend keys correspond to maximum likelihood $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textup  {mle}}_{n,m}$ (MLE), majority vote $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textup  {mv}}_{n,m}$ (MV), hard-labeled Dawid-Skene (DS) and GLAD crowdsourced estimators $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textsc  {ds}}_{n,m}$ and $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textsc  {glad}}_{n,m}$, and soft-labaled Dawid-Skene (DS prob) and GLAD (GLAD prob) estimators $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textsc  {ds-p}}_{n,m}$ and $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \theta $}\mathaccent "0362{\theta }^{\textsc  {glad-p}}_{n,m}$. (a) Comparison of methods using hard labels. (b) Comparison with crowdsourced estimated soft-labels. (c) Number of labelers $m$ versus test error for median accuracy $p = .105$ (noisy labelers). (d) Number of labelers $m$ versus test error for median accuracy $p = .4$. Both (c) and (d) report 95\% error bars over the trials.}}{35}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:semisynthetic}{{2}{35}{Experiments on semisynthetic CIFAR-10 dataset. Median labeler accuracy represents the median of $p_i = \max _y \softmax (\alpha f(x_i))_y$ on the training data. Results are averaged over $20$ trials, and vertical axes give mis-classification rate from (synthetic) ground-truth labels on held-out test set. Legend keys correspond to maximum likelihood $\what {\theta }^{\textup {mle}}_{n,m}$ (MLE), majority vote $\mve $ (MV), hard-labeled Dawid-Skene (DS) and GLAD crowdsourced estimators $\dse $ and $\glade $, and soft-labaled Dawid-Skene (DS prob) and GLAD (GLAD prob) estimators $\dspe $ and $\gladpe $. (a) Comparison of methods using hard labels. (b) Comparison with crowdsourced estimated soft-labels. (c) Number of labelers $m$ versus test error for median accuracy $p = .105$ (noisy labelers). (d) Number of labelers $m$ versus test error for median accuracy $p = .4$. Both (c) and (d) report 95\% error bars over the trials}{figure.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:semisynthetic@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][28][]35}{}{}{}}
